{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/995005-bluebooking-the-astral","id":995005,"title":"Bluebooking the Astral","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-28T19:18:16-07:00","id":995005,"title":"Bluebooking the Astral","content":"I've been working on a project to design a unified, flexible system of system-independent for magic, and some other stuff got swept up into the project. <br /> <br /> One of those things is working out a version of the astral/dream that's different from mage's cosmology, and can be used by any splat. One of the main parts of it is that there's no Temenos. I'm keeping that as being part of Mage's thing. It's not that it isn't cool, but it gets to the point where it starts to overlap a bit with other stuff, including Arcadia. And I'm going for a more cosmic horror tone, so I like the idea of humanity not having its own special imagination realm, and the closest thing it has to that is the playground of mad child-gods. But I'm getting off topic (and I really love Mage and the astral). <br /> <br /> So, basically, there's no longer a Temenos, only the Primordial Dream and individual dreams. Keeping the Primordial lets us keep Beast, and keeping individual dreams keeps changeling. Another idea I'm going with from Beast is that the Primordial Dream is connected to the various other supernatural realms- the Hedge, the Shadow, the underworld, and any others. It can also provide passage into alternate universe shards and time splinters, but the Machine really isn't fond of this, since it likes keeping those things apart, but it can't keep people from going through the cracks. I'm keeping it as a possible because of the story potential- someone stuck in a time splinter realizes that they're stuck there when someone starts psychically contacting them via dreams. <br /> <br /> The main crunchy bits we need are some merits to deal with dreamwalking, and what rolls it takes to move around. I'm working on devotions for vampires to access dreams in another thread, and once changeling comes out there'll be stuff there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T23:10:49-07:00","id":995090,"title":"","content":"With the mortal merits for dreamwalking, make sure you build them off the Lucid Dreamer merit from changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:28:36-07:00","id":995211,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't take ou the Temenos. It could easily work as a transition between realities, and it have its own merit. The Temenos does seem too similar to the Hedge on some features, and to the Shadow on a lot of others. But those are ultimately alien realms that only superficially take on humanized features, while the Temenos is human-defined.<br /> <br /> Or so it seems.<br /> <br /> For the Cosmic Horror stuff, what will bring the chills will be the relation of the Temenos with other realms, and how it can indicate that the Temenos itself isn't neither as human-defined as it seems at first, nor only human-occupied. And also how it is dotted of traps that can lead you to the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> As examples of how to use the Temenos with cosmic horror, I have personally two indications. The first is the game trilogy The Deepest Sleep, from Armor Games (it is free to play on their site or in Kongregate). The second is from the father of Cosmic Horror, H. P. Lovecraft's &quot;The Dream Quest of Unknown Kadath&quot; and others of Lovecraft's Dream books. For all intents and purposes, his stories happen mostly on the Temenos, with a good measure of connections both to the Anima Mundi as to <i>other, non-human Temenos</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:01:24-07:00","id":995336,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I could easily do any of that with the Primordial Dream or the Hedge. I'm kind of fine with keeping the Temenos as Mage's thing. It works spectacularly there, and there's a ton you can do with it there, but outside of Mage I feel like there are other things that can occupy its role pretty well. <br /> <br /> Basically, if I want to do something with the Temenos, and I do think it's a very neat idea, I'd go with it in Mage. Though I am going to be adapting some of the Temenos stuff, but moving it to the Hedge or the Primordial Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}